module latte_client
kind library

# The browser half of an execution boundary: the runtime that owns a `client`
# region's components, renders them, diffs them and hands the edits to the
# page's own applier.
#
# A SIBLING module and not a package under `latte/`, for the reason
# `latte_app` is one: a package under a module may not import its own module
# root, and this needs `Renderer`, `Builder`, `RenderMode` and the wire
# encoder — all of which live at that root.
#
# It imports NOTHING but latte and std.reflect. In particular it does not
# import `latte.browser`: that package is the canvas target's host and pulls
# CanvasKit, the scene graph, the layout engine and the paint stack with it,
# none of which an HTML page has any use for. The few bytes of pointer
# handling this module needs it declares itself, in `text.b`, beside a note
# saying where the other copy is.
#
# Nothing an HTML server links ever names this module, so a native build of an
# application carries none of it.
require path ".."
